{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk dominates in clear, safe states; move_forward is used for short progress; recovery turns are chosen deterministically based on obstacle location; full_rotate is reserved for rare, persistent blockage. All obstacle events force a recovery turn before returning to exploration. The design avoids oscillation and overuse of full_rotate, and ensures all uncontrollable events are handled in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate motion and perception in the plant: all controllable actions are one-shot, all sensor events are uncontrollable.",
    "Specification ensures: (1) random_walk is preferred in clear/search states, (2) move_forward is used for short progress, (3) recovery turns are deterministic and obstacle-aware, (4) full_rotate is only used as a last resort, (5) no unsafe or oscillatory behaviors."
  ],
